# Research Papers

A curated collection of research papers related to cascading failures, error propagation, reliability, reasoning, tool use, evaluation, and multi-agent systems.

---

## 1. Foundational Reasoning & Agent Architectures

### Chain-of-Thought Prompting

- **Paper:** *Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models*
- **Authors:** Jason Wei et al.
- **Year:** 2022
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2022
- **Link:** [Paper / DOI](https://doi.org/10.52202/068431-1800)
- **Why it matters:** Establishes the importance of intermediate reasoning steps for complex tasks and provides a foundation for understanding multi-step reasoning trajectories.

### ReAct

- **Paper:** *ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models*
- **Authors:** Shunyu Yao et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** ICLR 2023
- **Link:** [Paper / DOI](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2210.03629)
- **Why it matters:** Combines reasoning with actions and environmental observations, making it highly relevant to multi-step agent trajectories and error propagation.

### Toolformer

- **Paper:** *Toolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools*
- **Authors:** Timo Schick et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2023
- **Link:** [Paper / DOI](https://doi.org/10.52202/075280-2997)
- **Why it matters:** Studies how language models select, invoke, and incorporate external tools, highlighting potential sources of errors between tool calls.

### Tree of Thoughts

- **Paper:** *Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models*
- **Authors:** Shunyu Yao et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2023
- **Link:** [Paper](https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/hash/271db9922b8d1f4dd7aaef84ed5ac703-Abstract.html)
- **Why it matters:** Explores multiple reasoning paths, evaluation, and backtracking, providing insight into how early reasoning choices can affect later outcomes.

### HuggingGPT

- **Paper:** *HuggingGPT: Solving AI Tasks with ChatGPT and its Friends in Hugging Face*
- **Authors:** Yongliang Shen et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2023
- **Link:** [Paper / DOI](https://doi.org/10.52202/075280-1657)
- **Why it matters:** Uses an LLM to plan tasks, select models, execute subtasks, and aggregate results, creating a multi-step pipeline where intermediate errors can propagate.

---

## 2. Self-Correction & Agent Reliability

### Reflexion

- **Paper:** *Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning*
- **Authors:** Noah Shinn et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2023
- **Link:** [Paper](https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/hash/1b44b878bb782e6954cd888628510e90-Abstract-Conference.html)
- **Why it matters:** Enables agents to learn from previous failures using verbal feedback and episodic memory, providing a mechanism for recovery from mistakes.

### Self-Refine

- **Paper:** *Self-Refine: Iterative Refinement with Self-Feedback*
- **Authors:** Aman Madaan et al.
- **Year:** 2023
- **Venue:** NeurIPS 2023
- **Link:** [Paper / DOI](https://doi.org/10.52202/075280-2019)
- **Why it matters:** Demonstrates iterative generation, self-feedback, and refinement as a way to detect and correct errors before they persist.

### CRITIC

- **Paper:** *CRITIC: Large Language Models Can Self-Correct with Tool-Interactive Critiquing*
- **Authors:** Zhibin Gou et al.
- **Year:** 2024
- **Venue:** ICLR 2024
- **Link:** [Paper](https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/hash/fef126561bbf9d4467dbb8d27334b8fe-Abstract-Conference.html)
- **Why it matters:** Uses external tools to verify model outputs and provide corrective feedback, demonstrating the value of independent validation in agent systems.

### Where LLM Agents Fail and How They Can Learn From Failures

- **Paper:** *Where LLM Agents Fail and How They Can Learn From Failures*
- **Authors:** Kunlun Zhu et al.
- **Year:** 2025
- **Venue:** arXiv preprint
- **Link:** [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25370)
- **Why it matters:** Directly investigates cascading failures in LLM agents and introduces AgentErrorTaxonomy, AgentErrorBench, and AgentDebug for failure classification, diagnosis, and recovery.

